            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1"
          ],
          "text": "Investigations showed a white cell count of 14.2 and CRP of 68; urine dipstick was negative. Ultrasound demonstrated free fluid in the right iliac fossa, with the appendix not well seen. He was managed with nil by mouth, IV fluids and IV co-amoxiclav, and proceeded to laparoscopic appendicectomy on 20/05. Operative findings confirmed an acutely inflamed appendix with no perforation; the procedure was uncomplicated with minimal estimated blood loss. He was discharged on 21/05.",
